  "reasoning": [
    "Inventory deduction and costing call the same BaseQuantityMilliUnits; null Yield ratio skips stock posting but marks costing incomplete, not divergent conversion formulas.",
    "Purchase, prep, packaging and inventory valuation use PurchaseLineTotal quantity*decimal unitcost/1000. Money.FromEgp is a distinct currency-boundary conversion; do not merge unlike units merely because both round.",
    "Sold-cost reporting multiplies rounded per-recipe cost by sold quantity; stock uses converted milliunits times quantity. Per-line/perportion versus aggregate rounding is a policy/regression question, not automatically a confirmed defect.",
    "Order packaging once per order is separate from per-item recipe packaging. Missing completeness is existing financial finding, not a new duplicate.",
    "Existing499.5->500,100/4->25 and null conversion tests inspected only, not run."
  ],
  "required_tests": [
    "Specify midpoint and perportion/aggregate rounding policy before arithmetic changes.",
    "Cross-check fractional multiportion recipes between stock/cost, unknown ratios, once-per-order packaging, range/overflow boundaries."
  ],
